                        "sense_id": "3f53cece-636d-37d0-8bd4-d78e801bc8a4",
                        "entry_id": "94224875-b3ba-3f81-bb1c-3f1743d9ca79",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A weakfish, a silvery edible American sciaenoid fish of species Cynoscion regalis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "22f67813-0f5f-415a-a7a3-34b55eb51284",
                                "sense_id": "3f53cece-636d-37d0-8bd4-d78e801bc8a4",
                                "text": "Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand. We spent consider'ble money getting 'em reset, and then a swordfish got into the pound and tore the nets all to slathers, right in the middle of the squiteague season."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17d4a239-190d-4d08-a4d1-fe4099e66711",
                                "sense_id": "3f53cece-636d-37d0-8bd4-d78e801bc8a4",
                                "text": "The Injuns get to Naturmitgefuhl by the metaphor of a family: if you don't throw the roe-plump squeteague back, that is a sort of nepoticide."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
